# freestone file access rules
#
# Each line is either:
#   + /absolute/path   — allow access to this path and everything below it
#   - /absolute/path   — deny access to this path and everything below it
#
# Rules are evaluated in order. The LAST matching rule wins.
# If no rule matches, access is DENIED (default deny).
#
# Paths must be absolute. Use path-component matching, not string prefix:
#   + /Users/kai         matches /Users/kai/file.txt
#   + /Users/kai         does NOT match /Users/kaizen/file.txt
#
# Examples:
#
# Allow access to your Documents folder:
# + /Users/YOU/Documents
#
# But deny access to a private subfolder:
# - /Users/YOU/Documents/private
#
# Allow access to a project directory:
# + /Users/YOU/projects/my-project
#
# Allow reading from /tmp:
# + /tmp
